 like a somewhat favorable national environment for Democrats. Ten raters and prediction markets all point the same direction, so a Republican hold is the clear expectation, with the polls' age keeping uncertainty elevated.", "watch": "Fresher polling showing Jenkins closing the gap, or a strong national Democratic wave in the final weeks, would be the main forces that could tighten this race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 67 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Mike Haridopolos (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Mike Haridopolos, a first-term Republican incumbent and former Florida Senate president, enters the general election as a clear favorite in this Republican-leaning Space Coast district. Jennifer Jenkins, a former Brevard County School Board member who switched targets after redistricting, has struggled to match his money or profile. The two July polls, one from a Republican-linked firm and one from a Democratic-leaning pollster, both showed Haridopolos ahead by about nine points.\n\nHaridopolos has raised $1.8 million to Jenkins' $727,000 and holds a wide cash advantage, and the U.S. Chamber has endorsed his re-election. Ten ratings outlets place the race in the Safe or Likely Republican column, and prediction markets give Jenkins only a small chance. The national environment may be friendlier to Democrats than in recent cycles, which could narrow the margin, but nothing in the available evidence suggests Jenkins has closed the gap so far.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0724, "margin": -8.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0723, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0928, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0611, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0442, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0553, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0651, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0689, "margin": -10.0}, {"date"